d I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That made `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` give `2.68` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, on branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed.\n- **PR:** #101 \u2014 https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system didn't recognise that ID. The fix follows what the test and the docstring both say.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}